WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.336 --> 00:00:06.706
Do you all want to know
what my favorite word is?

00:00:06.722 --> 00:00:08.040
(Laughter)

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.275
It's the F word.

00:00:09.291 --> 00:00:10.559
(Audience: Yeah!)

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:12.411
Some people think it's a little dirty.

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:14.780
Others really like to throw it around.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.933
Oh, y’all thought I meant “fuck”?

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.218
(Laughter)

00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:20.703
No, no, no, no, no.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.872
My favorite word is “fandom.”

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.591
This talk is about fandom

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:28.210
and how fandom can enrich your life

00:00:28.244 --> 00:00:30.346
and build a community of people

00:00:30.362 --> 00:00:32.915
that you might not have
always talked to, right?

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.584
But I'm sure when you all think of fandom,

00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:40.306
y'all think nerds and cosplay
and fan fiction and neck beards

00:00:40.322 --> 00:00:42.324
and people in dark basements and stuff.

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:43.726
And all that is true.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:44.894
(Laughter)

00:00:45.728 --> 00:00:49.598
But you also probably think
about America's ass.

00:00:49.632 --> 00:00:52.268
(Laughter)

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:53.586
I do.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:57.757
(Laughter and cheers)

00:00:57.773 --> 00:01:00.743
And yes, fandom is all of this stuff,

00:01:00.776 --> 00:01:05.097
but it is actually a community
of people that share a passion.

00:01:06.398 --> 00:01:10.069
Fandom is a community of people
that share a passion.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.422
Right?

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:15.908
But like all things,
a there's a spectrum, right?

00:01:15.925 --> 00:01:21.781
You have your casual fans,
your fans, your hardcore fans,

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:23.916
and then you have your fanatics.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.754
And it can get really ugly,
just like that ugly thing.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.673
Every time I see it, I run scared.

00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:35.528
Sorry to all my Phillies fans,
it's ugly, right?

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.664
But I want to talk about the difference
between being a fan

00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:40.933
and being a fanatic, right?

00:01:43.252 --> 00:01:47.740
Fans want to bring in joy.

00:01:47.756 --> 00:01:50.860
They want to share stuff
as much as possible with you, right?

00:01:50.893 --> 00:01:52.178
Fanatics are --

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:56.232
And I know I watched Obi-Wan last night,
so "Star Wars" is on the brain --

00:01:57.516 --> 00:02:00.669
But fanatics are those "Star Wars" fans

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:03.506
that chased two grown women
off of the internet

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:08.344
because they gave the Millennium
Falcon to a girl, right.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.862
They weren't happy about that.

00:02:09.895 --> 00:02:11.380
Those are fanatics.

00:02:11.413 --> 00:02:12.832
We want to be fans.

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:15.851
We don't want to be fanatics, right?

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.637
Because fans create worlds.

00:02:19.155 --> 00:02:22.474
Once the story is over,
once the movie is done,

00:02:22.491 --> 00:02:24.276
they want to keep it going.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:30.633
So they start to create cosplay,
fan fiction, video games.

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:34.904
I mean, I myself have a lot
of feelings and fandoms,

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.824
so I have a newsletter that I write
whenever I remember to write it.

00:02:39.141 --> 00:02:42.962
(Laughter)

00:02:42.978 --> 00:02:46.348
And also, because we're friends here,

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:47.516
I cosplay.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.018
(Laughter)

00:02:49.051 --> 00:02:52.471
I'm not new to this,
I'm true to this, right.

00:02:52.504 --> 00:02:57.860
I wanted to still still engage
with all of the worlds that I love,

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.461
even though the movie was over.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:05.201
Fans aren't gatekeepers.

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:08.153
Y'all can clap.

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:13.209
(Applause)

00:03:13.242 --> 00:03:16.011
We all have that friend
that watches us watch a movie

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:18.814
because they want us to like
the same part that they like.

00:03:18.847 --> 00:03:20.332
(Laughter)

00:03:20.349 --> 00:03:21.717
That is a fan.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:25.654
Fanatics are those people who quiz me
when I come into a comic book store

00:03:25.688 --> 00:03:27.856
thinking because I look like this,

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.761
that I can't know about comics, right?

00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:38.734
And fans learn life lessons from some
of the nerdiest places, right?

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:43.639
So for a quick example, how many
Blazers fans are here?

00:03:43.672 --> 00:03:47.026
(Cheers and applause)

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:48.310
Right.

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:50.396
Y'all are really patient people, I'm sure.

00:03:50.412 --> 00:03:52.481
(Laughter)

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.650
Y'all will continue to be patient.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:58.404
With that number seven pick,
y’all got, sucks for y’all.

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:01.924
(Laughter)

00:04:04.576 --> 00:04:07.880
Or if you were an Oregon women's
Ducks fan, which we all should be --

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:11.200
(Cheers and applause)

00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:16.789
You probably understand
the importance of women in power,

00:04:16.822 --> 00:04:19.892
the value of women in sports

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:22.494
and you're probably just
overall a much better person.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:26.582
(Laughter)

00:04:30.319 --> 00:04:34.056
Because fandom when harnessed is greater
than any box office number.

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:38.827
Right, fandom when harnessed is greater
than any box office number.

00:04:39.561 --> 00:04:44.650
You meet people who you might have not
necessarily always talk to, right?

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:47.386
You learn from so many different people

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:50.873
and you learn a lot of things
from these things that you love so much.

00:04:50.889 --> 00:04:53.559
Whether or not you realize it, right?

00:04:53.575 --> 00:04:57.713
Think about what you put
on your locker when you were a teenager

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:01.984
or in your three-ring binder

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:05.070
or even on your phone
background right now.

00:05:05.688 --> 00:05:09.525
Something somewhere has inspired you

00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:13.679
or guided you along this journey
called life, right?

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:16.432
So I'm going to give you all ten things --

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:18.600
I have a lot of fandoms,
I have a lot of them,

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:21.904
but I'm going to give you ten things
that my fandoms have taught me.

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:26.342
Number one, Storm from the "X-Men,"

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:28.043
y'all should be clapping right now.

00:05:28.077 --> 00:05:32.264
(Applause and cheers)

00:05:32.281 --> 00:05:35.784
She is the leader of the X-Men.

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:38.370
As a young Black girl seeing this tall,

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:40.973
beautiful Black woman
with all this white hair

00:05:40.989 --> 00:05:44.193
and a very operatic voice leading the way,

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:49.214
it was very impactful
for a Fox Kids Saturday morning.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.018
That's my son.

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:55.754
(Applause and laughter)

00:05:56.839 --> 00:06:01.160
“Star Wars” taught me that my world
can be as big as a galaxy far, far away.

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:04.730
Whether that is real or fake.

00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:10.069
My world can be much bigger than just
the six blocks that I call my home.

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:13.105
Wonder Woman --

00:06:13.122 --> 00:06:15.841
(Cheers and applause)

00:06:15.874 --> 00:06:20.245
Taught me that my body at any sculpt,
at any shape is beautiful, right?

00:06:20.262 --> 00:06:22.047
Wonder Woman spent her entire life --

00:06:22.064 --> 00:06:23.265
Y'all can clap.

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:26.452
(Applause)

00:06:26.485 --> 00:06:29.071
Wonder Woman spent
her entire life training for battle.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:30.823
She was not going to be a size zero.

00:06:30.839 --> 00:06:33.008
She was going to have
quadriceps and deltoids.

00:06:33.041 --> 00:06:35.444
I learned that word
a couple of weeks ago, deltoid.

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:37.212
(Laughter)

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:39.164
And she was going to look strong

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:41.850
and look beautiful while doing it.

00:06:43.185 --> 00:06:44.570
Alright, the fourth one.

00:06:44.586 --> 00:06:50.392
(Cheers and applause)

00:06:50.426 --> 00:06:53.695
Venus and Serena,
as any Black girl, specifically --

00:06:53.712 --> 00:06:55.114
We were forced to watch them,

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:56.965
whether or not we liked tennis or not.

00:06:56.965 --> 00:06:59.034
(Laughter)

00:06:59.034 --> 00:07:02.621
It's also because it came on cable
so you didn't have to, like, look for it.

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:09.228
But my North Star as a big sister
has always been these two.

00:07:09.261 --> 00:07:14.583
Because when the world was against them,
they always had each other.

00:07:14.616 --> 00:07:18.454
So whether or not I am being
a good sister in the moment,

00:07:18.487 --> 00:07:20.556
that is what I always look towards.

00:07:23.008 --> 00:07:24.159
(Applause)

00:07:25.043 --> 00:07:26.211
All right.

00:07:26.228 --> 00:07:30.599
Sneakers taught me the importance
of quality and detail, and nerds --

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:32.634
Sneaker heads, you all are nerds.

00:07:32.651 --> 00:07:37.773
Nobody cares about quality leather
from 1987 to 2022 except y'all.

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:39.491
Y'all need to just accept it.

00:07:39.508 --> 00:07:41.443
(Laughter)

00:07:42.244 --> 00:07:43.662
"Harry Potter" fan fiction --

00:07:43.679 --> 00:07:46.048
(Cheers and applause)

00:07:46.064 --> 00:07:49.518
Taught me that I could write
myself into any story.

00:07:49.551 --> 00:07:52.037
Those books are about this big

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:54.606
and Black people
had about what, eight words?

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:55.891
(Laughter)

00:07:55.924 --> 00:07:59.411
So I wanted to fill in those gaps
and I was very good at it too.

00:07:59.428 --> 00:08:01.813
Also wrote some smut,
you can look for that later.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:04.816
(Laughter)

00:08:04.833 --> 00:08:06.018
“Sailor Moon” ...

00:08:06.051 --> 00:08:08.637
(Cheers and applause)

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.390
Taught me the power of female friendships.

00:08:12.991 --> 00:08:14.209
That's it.

00:08:14.226 --> 00:08:17.029
(Applause)

00:08:18.263 --> 00:08:20.716
And now, this isn't really a lesson,

00:08:20.749 --> 00:08:23.402
but my father is a massive nerd

00:08:23.418 --> 00:08:28.824
and he would see me glomming on
to these superheroes, Storm,

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:31.393
and he would be like,
"Well, what about Black Panther?

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.645
What about Luke Cage?
What about Misty Knight?"

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:36.031
And in doing that,
he was trying to teach me, yes,

00:08:36.064 --> 00:08:39.751
you can love everything that is current,
but you have to know about your past.

00:08:39.768 --> 00:08:43.488
And so showing me all of these Black
superheroes from the '70s,

00:08:43.505 --> 00:08:45.507
from the '60s,

00:08:45.541 --> 00:08:47.376
kind of led me through life.

00:08:47.392 --> 00:08:50.329
And now I'm a nerd here talking to you
all here, so blame him.

00:08:51.763 --> 00:08:52.931
Boy bands.

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:55.400
(Applause)

00:08:55.417 --> 00:08:58.537
B2K specifically, taught me
to scream really loud.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:01.723
(Laughter)

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:03.058
Then Chyna ...

00:09:03.091 --> 00:09:06.028
(Cheers and applause)

00:09:06.044 --> 00:09:09.998
Taught me that I can be
the ninth wonder of the world,

00:09:10.015 --> 00:09:13.368
that I can stand in a ring
or an office room

00:09:13.402 --> 00:09:15.120
or here on this red carpet

00:09:15.137 --> 00:09:18.357
and take command, right?

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.809
Because in a lot of rooms,

00:09:20.826 --> 00:09:22.711
I will probably be the only woman.

00:09:22.744 --> 00:09:24.763
I will probably be the only Black person.

00:09:24.796 --> 00:09:27.766
I'm for damn sure probably
going to be the only Black woman.

00:09:27.799 --> 00:09:29.768
So people are going to look at me anyway.

00:09:29.801 --> 00:09:31.320
I should have something to say.

00:09:31.353 --> 00:09:33.639
I should be able to take center stage.

00:09:33.655 --> 00:09:39.678
(Applause)

00:09:39.695 --> 00:09:44.700
So listen, don't be afraid of the F word.

00:09:44.716 --> 00:09:47.152
Because when you love
what you love out loud,

00:09:47.169 --> 00:09:49.304
that is audacious.

00:09:49.321 --> 00:09:53.041
When you love what you love
unapologetically,

00:09:53.058 --> 00:09:54.242
it is beautiful.

00:09:54.259 --> 00:09:56.161
All right, so fuck it, y'all, be a fan.

00:09:56.178 --> 00:09:58.630
(Cheers and applause)

